# The share images were renamed to force LinkedIn, WhatsApp and iMessage to
# re-fetch them. Those caches key on the image URL and hold for days, so the
# old filename was still serving the retired tagline long after the file that
# carried it was replaced. The old paths 301 so nothing already indexed 404s.
/assets/og-image.png                               /assets/og-image-v2.png        301
/assets/og-image-es.png                            /assets/og-image-es-v2.png     301

# The favicon was a black three-pointed spike left over from a template, and
# browsers pin a favicon far longer than the four hours the asset header asks
# for. Renaming it is the only reliable way to make a tab let go. The bare
# /favicon.ico is here because crawlers and older browsers ask for it at the
# root whether or not the page declares one — it was answering 404.
/favicon.ico                                       /assets/favicon-v2.ico         301
/assets/favicon.ico                                /assets/favicon-v2.ico         301

# Repo files that are not pages. There is no build step, so the repo root is the
# deploy directory and everything tracked in it answers 200 on the marketing
# domain — the worker source, the local preview server, the package manifest.
# They belong in the public repo; they do not belong on jldatrum.com. Pages does
# not accept a bare 404 status here, so these 301 to the real 404 page.
/worker/*                                          /404                           301
/tools/*                                           /404                           301
/package.json                                      /404                           301
/.claude/*                                         /404                           301
/.gitignore                                        /404                           301
